WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:08.656
If you are a full-time employee, your timecard fills itself in every Monday morning, based on your standard schedule.

00:00:08.656 --> 00:00:13.461
If your hours differ, just edit the blocks that are wrong, or add extra hours.

00:00:14.811 --> 00:00:17.695
Interns and part-time employees are different.

00:00:17.695 --> 00:00:23.088
Their timecards start empty, so they create their own time blocks for each pay period.

00:00:24.438 --> 00:00:26.775
Submit as it is when your hours match.

00:00:26.775 --> 00:00:31.203
If you worked overtime or had a schedule change, edit before you submit.

00:00:31.203 --> 00:00:36.491
And if you need to fix something later, adjustments are allowed for up to ninety days.

00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:42.586
Record every absence in Workday too, such as Time2Give or jury duty.

00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:46.353
Time worked and time off both belong on your timecard.

00:00:47.703 --> 00:00:52.624
On-call time starts with your leader, who marks you as eligible in Workday.

00:00:52.624 --> 00:00:58.202
Once that is set, record your on-call hours in the on-call sections of your timecard.

00:00:58.202 --> 00:00:58.792
Not sure?

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.842
Ask your leader.
